# {{name}}

Maven project for dicoogle-next plugins.

- Project id: `{{id}}`
- Maven coordinates: `{{groupId}}:{{artifactId}}:{{version}}`
- Parent: `{{parentGroupId}}:{{parentArtifactId}}:{{parentVersion}}`

This project was created by the `init` command. Add plugin modules with
`java --project`.

## Prerequisites

Java {{javaVersion}} and Maven {{mavenMinimum}} or newer are required. The
dicoogle-next parent enforces these versions, so an older JDK or Maven fails the
build. This generated project has no Maven wrapper; use `mvn` from `PATH`.

The dicoogle-next parent and SDK are not published to a remote repository. Install
them from a dicoogle-next checkout first:

```bash
cd /path/to/dicoogle-next/backend
./mvnw -B -ntp -N install
./mvnw -B -ntp -pl dicoogle-next-sdk -am install
```

If you need to run the prebuilt application, install the full backend so the
application jar and its built-in modules are present in `~/.m2`:

```bash
./mvnw -B -ntp install
```

## Add a plugin

Run the bootstrap tool from this project root with `--project .`:

```bash
node /path/to/dicoogle-plugin-bootstrap/bin/dicoogle-plugin-bootstrap.mjs java \
  --id my-store \
  --family storage \
  --readable \
  --project .
```

The generator writes the module under `plugins/<artifactId>` and adds a
`<module>plugins/<artifactId></module>` entry to this project's `pom.xml`.
Use `--dry-run` to inspect the generated files without writing anything.

Build the project:

```bash
mvn -B -ntp package
```

## Run the prebuilt app with plugin jars

The dicoogle-next application artifact is a Spring Boot executable jar. Use
`PropertiesLauncher` and `loader.path` to add plugin jars from this project:

```bash
java \
  -Dloader.path="plugins/my-store/target/dicoogle-next-storage-my-store-0.0.1-SNAPSHOT.jar" \
  -cp "$HOME/.m2/repository/org/dicoogle/dicoogle-next/0.0.1-SNAPSHOT/dicoogle-next-0.0.1-SNAPSHOT.jar" \
  org.springframework.boot.loader.launch.PropertiesLauncher \
  --app.storage.my-store.enabled=true
```

Use the property prefix that matches the generated module (`app.storage.<id>`,
`app.query.<id>`, or `app.service.<id>`). Generated plugins are disabled by
default, so the `enabled` property is required.

{{#if runVerified}}The run method above was verified against dicoogle-next
`0.0.1-SNAPSHOT`: the generated storage plugin appeared in
`/api/system/plugins` and its scheme was reported in the startup log.{{/if}}{{#unless runVerified}}The run method above is **unverified** in this environment.
Check it against your dicoogle-next build before relying on it.{{/unless}}

## Multi-module layout

```text
.
  pom.xml                 # this aggregator project
  plugins/
    my-store/
      pom.xml             # plugin module, parented to dicoogle-next
      src/...
```

Plugin modules inherit directly from
`{{parentGroupId}}:{{parentArtifactId}}:{{parentVersion}}` with an empty
`<relativePath/>`, so they resolve the parent and the
`{{sdkArtifactId}}:{{sdkVersion}}` SDK from the local Maven repository.
